    <string name="guide_title_xiaomi">On your Xiaomi (HyperOS / MIUI)</string>
    <string name="guide_title_samsung">On your Samsung</string>
    <string name="guide_title_huawei">On your Huawei / Honor</string>
    <string name="guide_title_oneplus">On your OnePlus / Oppo / Realme</string>
    <string name="guide_title_other">On your phone</string>
    <string name="guide_xiaomi">1. Autostart: Settings → Apps → Manage apps → ElTouro → switch Autostart on (button “Autostart” below).\n2. Battery: in the same app info → Battery saver → “No restrictions”.\n3. Location: app info → Permissions → Location → “Allow all the time” and “Use precise location”.\n4. Lock the app: open recent apps, press and hold ElTouro → tap the lock. Then HyperOS does not clear it away.\n5. Do not ride in ultra battery saver – it stops everything.</string>
    <string name="guide_samsung">1. Settings → Apps → ElTouro → Battery → “Unrestricted”.\n2. Settings → Battery → Background usage limits: ElTouro must not be under “Sleeping apps” or “Deep sleeping apps”; best add it to “Never sleeping apps”.\n3. Location: app info → Permissions → Location → “Allow all the time”, “Use precise location” on.</string>
    <string name="guide_huawei">1. Settings → Battery → App launch → ElTouro: switch “Manage automatically” off and all three switches on (auto-launch, secondary launch, run in background).\n2. Location: app info → Permissions → Location → “Allow all the time”.\n3. In recent apps, pull ElTouro down to lock it.</string>
    <string name="guide_oneplus">1. Settings → Apps → ElTouro → Battery usage: “Allow background activity” and “Allow auto launch” on.\n2. Location: app info → Permissions → Location → “Allow all the time”.\n3. Lock ElTouro in recent apps (menu above the app → Lock).</string>
    <string name="guide_other">1. Switch battery optimization off for ElTouro (button above).\n2. Location → “Allow all the time” and precise location.\n3. Keep battery saver off during the ride.</string>
